<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 2-year note coupon rises to 13.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Philippine 2-year note coupon rises to 13.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The coupon rate on the Philippines' fixed rate two-year notes rose to 13.75 percent from 13.50 during the regular monthly auction, the Bureau of Treasury said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Rates accepted by the Bureau of Treasury ranged from 13.125 to 13.75 percent, with the average at 13.646 percent.</p>
<p>The auction generated 5.372 billion pesos worth of bids, of which 3.0 billion pesos were accepted.</p>
<p>Dealers said the recent tightness at the money market caused the rise in rates on two-year notes.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
